# Security

Controlled by one property: `petclinic.security.enable` (**default `false`** — the whole API is
public out of the box).

## Three configurations, two always loaded

| Class | Condition | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `WebSecurityConfig` | **none — always active** | permit-all + a CORS policy that never applies |
| `DisableSecurityConfig` | `enable=false` | permit-all |
| `BasicAuthenticationConfig` | `enable=true` | HTTP Basic + JDBC auth, activates `@PreAuthorize` |

`WebSecurityConfig` has no `@ConditionalOnProperty`, so **two `SecurityFilterChain` beans always
exist**, both matching `/**`. Which one wins depends on bean ordering, not on anything explicit.

> **After changing any class in `security/`, re-verify both authentication and CORS.** Nothing
> in the code pins the ordering, so a refactor can silently make a secured build permit-all.
> Test with: `java -jar target/*.jar --server.port=9977 --petclinic.security.enable=true`

## Rules

1. **Never store a password unencoded.** `UserServiceImpl.saveUser` currently persists
   `getPassword()` verbatim (`AUTH-03`), and `POST /users` echoes it back (`AUTH-04`). Do not
   copy either pattern. Note `users.password` is `VARCHAR(20)` — too small for a bcrypt hash
   (`AUTH-06`), so encoding needs a schema change first.
2. Seed credentials are `admin` / `{noop}admin`. The `{noop}` prefix is load-bearing: a password
   stored without an encoder prefix creates a user that **cannot log in**.
3. Roles are referenced through the `Roles` bean, never as string literals:
   `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`. The model is flat — `ADMIN` does **not**
   inherit the others, and there is no per-record ownership.
4. Role names are persisted with the `ROLE_` prefix, applied by `UserServiceImpl`, not the mapper.
5. **CORS is contradictory.** `WebSecurityConfig` restricts origins to `localhost:4444` and
   omits `DELETE`, but the controller `@CrossOrigin` annotations win and allow everything
   (`AUTH-09`). Fix by removing one of the two — do not add a third mechanism.
6. Enabling security also 401s Swagger UI, `v3/api-docs` and `actuator/health` (`AUTH-08`), and
   breaks the SPA entirely, which has no auth code (`AUTH-07`).

Full detail: `docs/baseline/AUTHENTICATION_BASELINE_PRD.md`.
